WEBVTT

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.080
My room?

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.630
<i>It was a dream cliché?<i></i></i>

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.720
Quit it! I'm still sleepy!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:26.180
I'm finally at the end of my great adventure
and got the ultimate pillow!

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.010
--Got it!

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.640
--What kind of adventure is that?!
--Got it!

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.560
It wasn't a dream...

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.770
That means...

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.660
Ryusei?!

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:09.990
Oh, Mahiru?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.540
--I thought you weren't coming.
--Sakuya! Where's Ryusei?!

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.830
Y-Yeah...

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:18.580
Sakuya!

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:19.830
Ow!

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.670
This vinyl tape will work right?

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.090
Ryusei!

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:25.970
Huh?

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.260
Oh, Mahiru! You came, after all?

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.100
What was the look earlier for?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.060
No, you just seemed so serious.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.600
I thought I'd follow along...

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.230
Ow, ow, ow! Sorry! Sorry!

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.810
Ryusei, is your neck all right?

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.900
Yeah. It's fine, it's fine.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:43.980
They called it a car accident,
but it barely nicked me.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.280
Car accident?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.400
Accidents are still pretty scary!

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.240
What are you talking about?! Yesterday...

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.700
Huh? A vampire magician?

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.500
Goodness, you're starting to talk like Sakuya.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.830
Also, you weren't with us yesterday.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:01.500
Huh?

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.170
Stop saying weird things.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.920
Come on, we have to prepare
for the school festival.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.170
Something's wrong.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.550
The vampire and I weren't there yesterday,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.800
and things have been forcefully wrapped up.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.220
--No one can tell me what's going on...
--Hey! It's crowded!

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.140
--Argh! I just don't get what's going on at all!
--Shut up. Don't flail around.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.520
I'm hungry!

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:20.940
There's no room!

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.610
When did this guy get in here?

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.150
I'm hungry! I wanna drink blood!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.570
Just a bit!

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:28.740
You're so noisy!

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.570
More importantly, can you
tell me what's going on?!

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.700
It's like yesterday didn't happen!

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:32.950
Hey, that boy...

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.830
That's a doll, right?

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.500
Ow, ow, ow! What are you doing, brat!

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.460
Someone like you should just
get murdered by Tsubaki!

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.130
Who is this Tsubaki he keeps talking about?

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.920
Kuro, do you have any idea?

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.970
An idea of someone who'd attack
such a good-willed cat like me?

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.090
Hey, are you mainly a vampire or a cat?

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.640
Meow.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:58.180
Thinking simply, this
Tsubaki person is our enemy,

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:02.650
and if we don't do something about him,
another vampire will attack...

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.860
Huh? A sunny shower?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.040
What's this?!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.160
Hey, you.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:26.210
Tell me an interesting story.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:30.590
I want to hear the most recent
and interesting story you know.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.720
The kitty he picked up was a vampire!

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:40.680
And the boy used the vampire to murder
a magician that pissed him off!

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.350
I have a feeling this is going to be a pain.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.940
Can it be, he's also...?

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.240
Not interesting at all.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.580
H-Hey! Don't hide!

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.250
Isn't he someone you know?!

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.590
Don't know him. He has a crazy look in his eyes.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.130
Hey, I was looking for this.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.630
Thanks for picking it up.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.100
You're late, Tsubakyun!

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.310
My shoulders got all stiff!

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.980
Tsubakyun?

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.940
But you saved me! Thanks, Tsubakyun.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.110
Tsubakyun. Wait, it can't be.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.480
No way, so soon?!

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.690
Hey, quit it. Don't think too deeply.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.570
We have to hurry and--

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:39.280
Right, I'm Tsubaki. So what?

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:43.500
I'm the one who picked
a fight with you. So what?

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:49.380
I'm the one who wants to kill lots
of vampires and humans. So what?

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.510
I'm very melancholy.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.680
Hey, Sleepy Ash of Sloth.
Tell me an interesting story.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.890
If you don't have one, let's have a war.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.980
Huh?! What are you saying?!

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.190
Come on, Big Brother.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.190
Big Brother?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.230
Kuro's little brother?

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.360
No. No. He must be mistaken.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:16.200
I don't know this guy.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.870
Terrible! So terrible!
So you don't know me either?

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:27.870
In the end, all of my Servamp siblings
didn't know who I was!

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.340
Hey, do you know how many Servamps there are?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.380
Huh?

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:39.050
There are seven.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.640
Right. Seven vampires.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:44.350
Sleepy Ash of Sloth.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.400
Old Child of Pride.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.770
Doubt Doubt of Envy.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.320
The Mother of Wrath

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.860
Lawless of Greed.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:57.700
World End of Gluttony

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.660
And then, All of Love of Lust.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:05.830
The ones called true vampires
are siblings of seven.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.750
But there is actually one more.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.510
I'm the eighth true vampire,
 the Servamp of Melancholy.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.500
I'm the eighth true vampire,
 the Servamp of Melancholy.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.960
My nickname is “Who is Coming.“

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.130
I'm the youngest sibling, Brother.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.930
Kuro has so many siblings...

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.050
Because he's a cat?

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.310
Wrong. And I'm the only cat in the group.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.690
See, I can transform into this.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.900
Ouch! Don't fight on top of me!

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.690
<i>A-A dog?</i>

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.860
So mean. I'm a fox. Calling me a dog.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.790
Not interesting at all.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:51.540
Tsubakyun, I wasn't able to murder
like you ordered because of them!

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:56.420
Tsubaki, are you killing people?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.460
So what if I am?

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:01.470
I don't like humans.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.220
Didn't you take down this vampire
because you didn't like him, too?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.810
Isn't it fair?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.690
Hey, do you know how many people
died in this town yesterday?

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.310
You don't know, right?

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:19.490
Then, it shouldn't matter to you
how many of those were murdered by us.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.450
What are you trying to do?!

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:24.410
Don't involve people
who have nothing to do with this!

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.410
Have nothing to do with this?

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:32.000
It's not interesting that some think
they have nothing to do with this.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.710
Especially...

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:39.660
You, Sleepy Ash.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.640
Well, Brother.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:51.020
Let's play!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:58.230
You all have forgotten. No, you want to forget.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:03.150
I want to have a great parade!

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:06.200
Call all seven siblings here for me.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:10.370
Teacher will be happier with more attendees.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:16.250
And all I want is for
this world to regret it all!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.300
Kuro! Drink my blood!

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.760
Don't want to!

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:26.890
I'm really sore today.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.470
That's the reason?!

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.810
<i>Kuro!</i>

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:40.320
I don't get it. A war? Why?!

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:43.900
<i>Kuro!</i>

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:48.120
Because it's interesting.
It doesn't matter who dies.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:52.750
Nothing matters as long as
it's interesting to me.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:57.540
What's with this guy?
He's not listening to my words at all.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.710
You don't understand how I feel.

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.720
Nobody knows who I am anyways.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.720
No one in this world can understand me anyways.

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:11.970
Huh? This feels familiar...

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:13.350
Why?

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.930
Mom.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:17.440
Are you really all right?

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.650
You can rest a few more days, you know.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.570
No. I'll go, Uncle.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:23.990
I'm fine.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.030
Mahiru, are you all right already?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:30.660
Tell me if you ever want to talk about anything.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:31.530
Koyu ki.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.490
Mahiru! Let's play soccer.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.660
I thought of a new technique!

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.040
Ryusei.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.250
Thanks, you two.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:42.460
But I have things to do, so I'm going home.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:43.590
What?

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.960
What?

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:47.340
Then, let's play tomorrow!

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.430
Mahiru?

00:10:56.140 --> 00:11:02.900
Mahiru. What's wrong?
Did something happen at school?

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.360
No. Nothing.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:08.950
Everyone was really nice.
They asked me to play, too.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.580
But I don't know why.
I just... don't feel like doing anything.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.370
How are you feeling right now?

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.870
If you don't understand what you're feeling,

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:22.880
the words of others will never reach you.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:28.300
Try giving it a name. That's a way
you can face those feelings.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:34.680
If you do, you'll be able to face
all sorts of feelings that come to you.

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:40.350
If you don't face it yourself first,
no one will be able to face you.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:45.360
Nothing is interesting to you,
because you aren't facing your feelings.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:51.950
You feel no one understands you,
because you don't want to face others.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.320
Huh?

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.920
Maybe 50. That's why I'm saying
we should have a war!

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.960
It's a method of communication!

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.590
A positive way of thinking!

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.550
You're wrong! If you want to
start a war, I'll stop you!

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:14.180
I have a way to face you, too!

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.430
If I name a Servamp and give them my blood,

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:22.690
they'll listen a little right?

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.270
I'm telling you to face me head-on!

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.610
I'll give you a name!

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:35.830
I see. But you'll die before then?

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.910
Get away, Mahiru!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.500
Huh? They got away.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.170
What a killjoy...

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.720
Is it okay to let them go, Tsubakyun?

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.220
We have to save fun things for later.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:58.180
My name is Tsubaki.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:00.600
Right, Teacher?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.190
Not interesting at all.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.820
Huh?! What?! What happened?!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:13.450
Ah, we were saved. Probably by another Servamp.

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.950
Another Servamp? Who?

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:18.950
Ah, probably...

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:20.950
Shirota Mahiru.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:27.000
Come with us. All of Love is calling for you.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.290
Me?

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.050
That's right.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.300
What a pain. I can't face this.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:35.220
Troublesome or not...

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:38.470
I'll have you come with me.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.810
I won't accept any other answer than yes.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:43.770
Cat.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:44.890
Cat.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.520
Are you All of Love?

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.610
No, I am Alicein Misono.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.690
Alicein Misono.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:56.360
I'm the Eve of the seventh Servamp, All of Love.

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:57.240
Eve?

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.660
That is what a master
contracted with a Servamp is called.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.080
So you're the same as me!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:06.670
So that guy has an Eve, too?

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:08.540
Huh? Huh?!

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:10.040
That's my room.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.460
Wow, the house is really far from the gate.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.720
I'm tired. Wait a moment.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.800
Where did you get that chair from?!

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:21.930
And we've only walked for five minutes
since we got out of the car!

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:27.140
Misono has a bit of
a weak body, Shirota Mahiru-kun.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.480
Huh?

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.610
What are you looking...?

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:34.360
I keep telling you not
to land on my hair, Lily!

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:36.150
Butterfly?

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:40.990
Nice to meet you.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.540
If you'd like, I'll go all out for you.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.160
Don't strip, pervert!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.380
I was thinking first impressions are important.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:54.630
This stripper here is
the Servamp of Lust, All of Love.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.680
My name is currently Snowlily.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.840
Please feel free to call me Lily.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:01.220
Don't strip!

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:03.720
You haven't changed at all.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:07.100
I'm glad to see you well, too.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:08.980
Now, please come in.

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.110
Bastard...

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:15.610
Actually, I helped out during
the magician case as well.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:18.030
I see. That's why everyone...

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.530
Thank you!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.490
I'm glad to meet an ally.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.290
There are a lot of things I want to ask...

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:28.290
First, will you please listen to our request?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:29.170
Huh?

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:33.290
I didn't go all out just from
the goodness of my heart.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.050
Lily.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:49.440
Huh?

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:54.570
Bastard, I heard you didn't launch
a single attack against Tsubaki.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:56.320
Misono! You know about Tsubaki, too?

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.490
Don't call my name so easily!

00:15:58.690 --> 00:15:59.360
Huh?

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:03.740
How pathetic. You don't understand
how to use a Servamp at all.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:04.870
Huh?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.200
Shirota Mahiru, become my servant.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:12.120
All your actions will be under
my orders from now on.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.330
Huh? Huh?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.500
I won't accept any answer other than yes.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:23.300
I'd like to resolve this peacefully if possible.

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:26.640
You'll listen to our request, right?

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:30.060
It's gotten troublesome again.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:33.270
So one-sided! Listen to what I have to say, too!

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.730
You aren't quick on the uptake.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.030
This is why I dislike commoners.

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:39.440
What?

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:43.360
I don't know just how rich you are,
but why are you so arrogant?!

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.780
No one would listen to you
after being dragged here

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:47.410
and demanded like that!

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.500
Bastard, how dare you talk to me like that!

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.910
Enough! Kuro, let's go home!

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:55.960
I thought I found an ally, too.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:57.340
What the hell is with him?!

00:16:58.420 --> 00:16:59.380
That guy...

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.800
Well, Misono. What shall we do?

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.600
Huh? So this isn't the way out?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:10.770
Looks like we're lost.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:18.020
What? So many...

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:24.530
Children? But this many...

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.450
It can't be that they're all Lily's kids?!

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.080
Even as Lust, that's way too many!

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.740
No, no. Impossible!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:32.660
Those children are my subclass.

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:34.170
Subclass?

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:38.500
Subclasses are lower vampires made by a Servamp.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:42.130
They follow the orders
of the vampire that creates them.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:45.970
Those children are vampires?

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:52.100
Tsubaki's vampires are killing subclasses
like these children first.

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:56.310
We know of two that have been
murdered just this week.

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:00.610
Do you know the game of chess?

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:01.980
Misono?

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:06.030
As the game progresses, the number
of pieces on the board decreases.

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:09.660
As long as the king survives, you win.

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:14.410
I don't think that is how
things should be in reality.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:20.090
I do not sit on the throne to be protected.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:26.260
That's why I need power. I need far more power.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:30.100
For what reason do you use your power?

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:30.760
Huh?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:34.100
There is only one chair for an Eve per Servamp.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:38.150
Do you have the resolve
and reason to sit in that chair?

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:43.230
My friend was attacked!

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.400
Shirota Mahiru.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:48.570
Will you please save the lonely Alice?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.450
You know.

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:57.210
Putting it simply, you just want
to protect everyone, right?

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:04.510
I don't think you have to be
the only person protecting these kids.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:07.880
Misono. Kuro and I will help you.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.720
Not as a servant, but as a friend.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.430
Don't involve me on your own.

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.600
If you dislike being called a servant,

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:19.650
I-I'll leave things at that.
Though it's the same, either way.

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.940
What are you laughing at, Lily?!

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:24.070
Don't run away!

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.900
Shirota Mahiru!

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.200
You still don't have a weapon, correct?

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:29.910
Weapon?

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.950
Do you plan on fighting vampires empty-handed?

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:37.370
An Eve can use a custom weapon
using their Servamp's power.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.620
There's something like that?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:43.840
It can't be helped.
I'll teach you how to use it.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:47.760
Yeah, please do so.
Please take care of me, Misono.

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:53.140
I found an ally who will fight with me.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:55.100
A great ally.

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.310
Huh? Mahiru?

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.650
That cat... did you start keeping it?

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:02.980
Huh? Yeah.

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:06.690
Be careful Mahiru. Black cats are bad luck.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:09.950
It's fine. It's just a normal cat.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.910
Just a cat, huh?

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.990
Oh, I think I'll buy this wristband.

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.160
Huh?!

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:17.200
I lost mine somewhere.

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.580
Um, no. If that's the case...

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:23.460
Aw, jeez! Here!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:24.790
Huh?

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.090
This is...

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:34.930
After you told me you lost it,
I happened to find one and bought it.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.760
I didn't have a good chance to give it to you...

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:37.770
Sakuyan.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:41.980
Isn't it weird, though?
It's not your birthday or anything!

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:43.770
Thank you, Sakuya.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:45.610
Stop it! It's embarrassing!

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.480
Say it more!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:56.950
Oh. No, it's nothing.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:21:00.790
Oh, could it be vampires? The rumors!

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:07.250
Sakuya, tell me if anything
strange happens to you.

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:09.460
I'll definitely do something about it.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:12.050
What are you, an exorcist?

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:16.010
But, haven't you been acting
weird lately, Mahiru?

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.600
Did something happen?

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:22.560
Have you been hiding something from me lately?

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:26.310
You're not lying to me are you?

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.650
What are you talking about?

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:37.910
Sakuya, don't worry. It'll be fine.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:39.410
See you later!

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:44.540
Well, it's a lie that Kuro is just a cat.

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.790
But I can't tell him that he's a vampire.

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:50.960
I was probably elated at the time.

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:55.260
I felt like I had received
the power to protect everything.

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:56.550
Just...

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:06.310
What did I think I was able to protect?
